  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Shelter Repair and Winterization Assistance for Families in Balkh, Jawzjan, Nuristan, Paktika and Parwan Provinces</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mid-Year 2022 Whole of Afghanistan Assessment findings indicated that 56 per cent of households in Afghanistan are living in partially damaged shelters and 18 per cent are living in significantly damaged shelters. People living in poor shelter conditions urgently need support for shelter improvements, heating materials and warm clothing before the onset of winter to reduce their exposure to health risks and other hazards. IOM continues to fill identified gaps with the provision of non-food items and emergency shelter in the affected districts. However, overall needs for transitional shelter and winterization assistance in the affected districts continue to grow considering the impact of earthquake and recent floods, vulnerabilities and winter approaching that confirms evident unaddressed needs of durable shelter interventions. In line with the Afghanistan Inter-Cluster Coordination Team winterization Plan (August 2022), IOM is providing assistance through the distribution of cash-for-shelter repairs/upgrade, cash-for-winterization (fuel/heating) and one-off direct cash transfers, complemented with winter clothing as well as blanket modules.</narrative>
  </description>
